            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Selbstlernendes Wörterbuch"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.self-learning-dictionary.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry self-learning-dictionary).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Automatically detects when you correct a dictation, adds the corrected word to your dictionary, and shows Undo. The Self-Learning Dictionary help article covers which apps it works in and how the judge runs on your Mac."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Erkennt automatisch, wenn du ein Diktat korrigierst, übernimmt das korrigierte Wort in dein Wörterbuch und zeigt „Rückgängig“ an. Im Hilfeartikel zum selbstlernenden Wörterbuch erfährst du, in welchen Apps es funktioniert und wie die Prüfung auf deinem Mac abläuft."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.dock-icon-and-window-in-front.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry dock-icon-and-window-in-front).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A Dock icon, and a window that opens in front"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein Symbol im Dock und ein Fenster im Vordergrund"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.dock-icon-and-window-in-front.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry dock-icon-and-window-in-front).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "EnviousWispr now shows in the Dock and in Command-Tab like any Mac app, and its window opens in front of what you were doing. On a Mac where you never moved it, the menu bar icon also starts further right, closer to the system icons, where it is easier to find. Prefer the menu bar alone? Switch off Show app in Dock in Settings, Appearance."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "EnviousWispr erscheint jetzt wie andere Mac-Apps im Dock und beim Wechseln mit Befehlstaste-Tab. Das Fenster öffnet sich vor deiner aktuellen Arbeit. Wenn du das Menüleistensymbol nie verschoben hast, erscheint es außerdem weiter rechts bei den Systemsymbolen und ist leichter zu finden. Du möchtest nur die Menüleiste nutzen? Deaktiviere „App im Dock anzeigen“ unter Einstellungen > Erscheinungsbild."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.mouse-wheel-scrolling-glides.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry mouse-wheel-scrolling-glides).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mouse wheel scrolling glides"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sanfter mit dem Mausrad scrollen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.mouse-wheel-scrolling-glides.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry mouse-wheel-scrolling-glides).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mouse wheel scrolling now moves farther per notch with a short smooth glide, while trackpad scrolling stays unchanged."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mit dem Mausrad scrollst du jetzt pro Rastung weiter und gleitest kurz sanft aus. Das Scrollen mit dem Trackpad bleibt unverändert."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.import-your-snippets.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry import-your-snippets).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Import your snippets"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Importiere deine Textbausteine"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.import-your-snippets.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry import-your-snippets).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bring snippets in from the file you exported, a CSV, a list you paste, or straight from Wispr Flow or TypeWhisper. You review the list before anything is saved, snippets you already have are skipped, and your keyword stays as it is."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Importiere Textbausteine aus einer exportierten Datei, einer CSV-Datei, einer eingefügten Liste oder direkt aus Wispr Flow oder TypeWhisper. Du prüfst die Liste, bevor etwas gespeichert wird. Vorhandene Textbausteine werden übersprungen und dein Schlüsselwort bleibt erhalten."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.say-slash-get-a-slash.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry say-slash-get-a-slash).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Say slash, get a slash"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sag „Slash“ und erhalte einen Schrägstrich"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.say-slash-get-a-slash.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry say-slash-get-a-slash).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Slash works with the spoken punctuation setting off: \"slash clear\" becomes /clear, \"command is slash wfp\" becomes command is /wfp, \"pros slash cons\" becomes pros/cons, and \"slash the budget\" stays words. Some verb uses, like \"slash prices\", can still become a symbol. Backslash still needs Convert spoken punctuation on. The Spoken punctuation and emoji help article has the details."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "„Slash“ funktioniert auch bei ausgeschalteter Option für gesprochene Satzzeichen: Aus „slash clear“ wird /clear, aus „command is slash wfp“ wird command is /wfp und aus „pros slash cons“ wird pros/cons. „Slash the budget“ bleibt Text. Bei manchen Verwendungen als Verb, etwa „slash prices“, kann trotzdem ein Zeichen entstehen. Für den umgekehrten Schrägstrich muss „Gesprochene Satzzeichen umwandeln“ weiterhin aktiviert sein. Einzelheiten stehen im Hilfeartikel zu gesprochenen Satzzeichen und Emoji."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.transcribe-a-file.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry transcribe-a-file).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Introducing \"Transcribe a File\""
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Neu: „Datei transkribieren“"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.transcribe-a-file.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry transcribe-a-file).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Historically, transcribing audio locally meant settling for messy, raw text full of filler words and false starts, unless you uploaded your private recordings to cloud servers. Transcribe a File changes that by running both speech transcription and intelligent AI polishing entirely offline. Drop in a single voice memo or queue up a massive archive of files to get back clean, structured text complete with speaker detection, automatic lists, and full edit history. You get publication-ready transcripts at scale without a single byte ever leaving your machine."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wer Audio bisher lokal transkribierte, bekam oft rohen Text voller Füllwörter und abgebrochener Sätze – außer die privaten Aufnahmen wurden in die Cloud geladen. „Datei transkribieren“ erledigt sowohl die Transkription als auch die intelligente KI-Nachbearbeitung vollständig offline. Füge eine einzelne Sprachnotiz hinzu oder stelle ein großes Dateiarchiv in die Warteschlange. Du erhältst sauberen, gegliederten Text mit Sprechererkennung, automatischen Listen und vollständigem Bearbeitungsverlauf. So entstehen auch in großer Zahl veröffentlichungsreife Transkripte, ohne dass ein einziges Byte deinen Mac verlässt."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.apple-intelligence-macos-27.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry apple-intelligence-macos-27).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apple Intelligence polish improved on macOS 27"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bessere Nachbearbeitung mit Apple Intelligence unter macOS 27"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.apple-intelligence-macos-27.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry apple-intelligence-macos-27).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "On macOS 27, Apple Intelligence now removes the opening ums, lays out spoken lists and resolves more of your self-corrections. Long dictations that fit its larger model are no longer skipped. The Apple Intelligence card in Settings shows which model is running and its capacity. On macOS 26 nothing changes."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Unter macOS 27 entfernt Apple Intelligence jetzt Fülllaute am Anfang, formatiert gesprochene Listen und berücksichtigt mehr deiner Selbstkorrekturen. Lange Diktate, die in das größere Modell passen, werden nicht mehr übersprungen. Die Apple Intelligence-Karte in den Einstellungen zeigt das verwendete Modell und seine Kapazität. Unter macOS 26 ändert sich nichts."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.capitalization-stays-on.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry capitalization-stays-on).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Improved capitalization when dictating into an existing sentence"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Bessere Großschreibung beim Fortsetzen eines Satzes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.capitalization-stays-on.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry capitalization-stays-on).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you dictate after words you already typed, EnviousWispr matches your capitalization. If the app was busy, that matching could switch itself off until you relaunched. It now stays on in far more cases."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wenn du nach bereits getippten Wörtern diktierst, passt EnviousWispr die Großschreibung an. War die App beschäftigt, konnte diese Anpassung bis zum nächsten Start ausfallen. Jetzt bleibt sie in deutlich mehr Fällen aktiv."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.measurements-keep-their-unit.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry measurements-keep-their-unit).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dictated measurements keep their unit"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Diktierte Messwerte behalten ihre Einheit"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.measurements-keep-their-unit.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry measurements-keep-their-unit).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Say \"the gap is 5 mm\" or \"120 mm Hg\" and the unit now comes through with the number."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sag „der Abstand beträgt 5 mm“ oder „120 mm Hg“: Die Einheit erscheint jetzt zusammen mit der Zahl."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.no-more-freeze-after-idle.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry no-more-freeze-after-idle).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "No more freeze after sitting idle"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Kein Hängenbleiben mehr nach einer Pause"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.no-more-freeze-after-idle.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry no-more-freeze-after-idle).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If EnviousWispr sat idle for a while, pressing the dictate key could silently freeze for a few seconds before anything happened. The speech engine now runs directly inside EnviousWispr instead of a separate helper that macOS could shut down behind its back, so that freeze is gone."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wenn EnviousWispr eine Weile inaktiv war, konnte nach dem Drücken der Diktiertaste einige Sekunden lang scheinbar nichts passieren. Die Spracherkennung läuft jetzt direkt in EnviousWispr statt in einem separaten Hilfsprozess, den macOS unbemerkt beenden konnte. Damit entfällt diese Verzögerung."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.spoken-addresses-more-languages.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry spoken-addresses-more-languages).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spoken email addresses convert in more languages' own words"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gesprochene E-Mail-Adressen in mehr Sprachen umwandeln"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.spoken-addresses-more-languages.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry spoken-addresses-more-languages).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When you dictate in English and say an address with another language's words for at and dot, such as \"marco arroba esempio punto com\", it comes back as marco@esempio.com. Addresses ending in a country domain such as .de, .nl or .fr now convert too."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wenn du auf Englisch diktierst und für „at“ und „dot“ Wörter aus einer anderen Sprache verwendest, etwa „marco arroba esempio punto com“, entsteht daraus marco@esempio.com. Auch Adressen mit Länderendungen wie .de, .nl oder .fr werden jetzt umgewandelt."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.pill-reduce-motion.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry pill-reduce-motion).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The recording pill honours Reduce Motion"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Aufnahmeanzeige beachtet „Bewegung reduzieren“"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.pill-reduce-motion.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry pill-reduce-motion).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "With Reduce Motion on in macOS, the recording pill no longer breathes, flashes or pulses. The colours stay so a warning still reads as a warning, and the lips still move with your voice."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wenn „Bewegung reduzieren“ in macOS aktiviert ist, atmet, blinkt und pulsiert die Aufnahmeanzeige nicht mehr. Die Farben bleiben erhalten, damit Warnungen erkennbar sind. Die Lippen bewegen sich weiterhin mit deiner Stimme."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Small things that now just work"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Kleine Dinge, die jetzt einfach funktionieren"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Eight fixes across dictation, paste and History."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Acht Korrekturen für Diktate, Einfügen und Verlauf."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.0" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 1 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Stalled transcription recovery: Canceling a dictation that fails to finish now halts the process immediately while preserving your recorded audio."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hängende Transkription: Wenn du ein Diktat abbrichst, das nicht fertig wird, stoppt der Vorgang sofort. Deine Aufnahme bleibt erhalten."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.1" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 2 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Decimal formatting: Numbers spoken digit by digit around a decimal point (e.g., \"two four oh seven point one two three\") now format properly as a single decimal number."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dezimalzahlen: Ziffer für Ziffer gesprochene Zahlen rund um ein Dezimalkomma werden jetzt korrekt als eine Dezimalzahl formatiert, etwa „zwei vier null sieben Komma eins zwei drei“."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.2" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 3 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quick Add persistence: Quick Add continues to display the heard phrase on screen even when nothing in your list matches it."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Schnell hinzufügen: Der erkannte Ausdruck bleibt sichtbar, auch wenn kein Eintrag in deiner Liste dazu passt."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.3" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 4 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Shortcut conflict priority: When the cancel shortcut shares a key combination with Quick Add, cancel now reliably takes priority."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tastenkürzelkonflikt: Wenn „Abbrechen“ und „Schnell hinzufügen“ dieselbe Tastenkombination verwenden, hat „Abbrechen“ jetzt zuverlässig Vorrang."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.4" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 5 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Paste timeout protection: Bringing an unresponsive target app to the front before pasting now aborts after 500 ms instead of freezing the app."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zeitlimit beim Einfügen: Reagiert die Ziel-App nicht, wird der Versuch, sie vor dem Einfügen nach vorn zu holen, nach 500 ms abgebrochen. EnviousWispr bleibt bedienbar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.5" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 6 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Safer crash recovery: Crash recovery retains the key to a saved recording until the audio file itself is confirmed safely removed."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sicherere Wiederherstellung: Nach einem Absturz bleibt der Schlüssel zu einer gespeicherten Aufnahme erhalten, bis das Löschen der Audiodatei bestätigt ist."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.6" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 7 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Process cleanup on launch: Any lingering background servers left over from an earlier session are automatically terminated on startup."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Aufräumen beim Start: Hintergrundserver aus einer früheren Sitzung werden beim Start automatisch beendet."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.small-things-that-now-just-work.bullet.7" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: point 8 of the list under one feature announcement (entry small-things-that-now-just-work).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "History type filters: History now distinguishes between Dictations (live keybind speech) and Transcripts (imported files). A new filter switch at the top of the list lets you quickly toggle between All, Dictations, and Transcripts."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Filter im Verlauf: Der Verlauf unterscheidet jetzt zwischen Diktaten über ein Tastenkürzel und Transkripten aus importierten Dateien. Oben in der Liste kannst du zwischen „Alle“, „Diktate“ und „Transkripte“ wechseln."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.model-lives-in-our-own-folder.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry model-lives-in-our-own-folder).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The speech model now lives in its own folder"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Sprachmodell hat jetzt einen eigenen Ordner"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.model-lives-in-our-own-folder.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry model-lives-in-our-own-folder).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "EnviousWispr keeps its speech model somewhere that belongs to it, and leaves every other app's files alone. If the model is already on your Mac it gets reused in seconds instead of downloaded again, even if you are offline."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "EnviousWispr speichert sein Sprachmodell in einem eigenen Ordner und lässt Dateien anderer Apps unangetastet. Liegt das Modell bereits auf deinem Mac, wird es in Sekunden wiederverwendet statt erneut heruntergeladen – auch offline."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.model-repairs-itself.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry model-repairs-itself).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A damaged speech model fixes itself"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein beschädigtes Sprachmodell repariert sich selbst"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.model-repairs-itself.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry model-repairs-itself).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If part of the speech model goes missing or gets corrupted, EnviousWispr repairs it on its own. Where a copy is already on your Mac it uses that one. Otherwise it fetches just the missing piece instead of the whole model."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Fehlt ein Teil des Sprachmodells oder ist er beschädigt, repariert EnviousWispr ihn selbst. Gibt es bereits eine Kopie auf deinem Mac, wird sie verwendet. Andernfalls lädt die App nur den fehlenden Teil statt des gesamten Modells."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.snippets.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry snippets).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Introducing \"Snippets\""
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Neu: „Textbausteine“"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.snippets.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry snippets).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Stop retyping the same information. Save your email address, LinkedIn, Calendly link, or common email templates as snippets. Speak your keyword followed by your customizable trigger phrase, and the text drops straight into your active cursor field. New installs come preloaded with six examples to help you get started. To set it up: Settings > Snippets."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tippe häufig verwendete Angaben nicht immer wieder neu. Speichere deine E-Mail-Adresse, einen LinkedIn- oder Calendly-Link oder häufige E-Mail-Vorlagen als Textbausteine. Sprich dein Schlüsselwort gefolgt von deinem anpassbaren Auslöser, und der Text erscheint direkt an der aktuellen Cursorposition. Bei neuen Installationen helfen dir sechs Beispiele beim Einstieg. Einrichtung: Einstellungen > Textbausteine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.eg1-1-2.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry eg1-1-2).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Introducing \"Email Formatting\" for EG-1"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Neu für EG-1: „E-Mail-Formatierung“"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.eg1-1-2.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry eg1-1-2).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "With EG-1, you can now dictate emails aloud and have them automatically converted into clean, ready-to-send formats. The model retains all its standard text-polishing capabilities, too."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Mit EG-1 kannst du E-Mails jetzt diktieren und automatisch in ein sauberes, versandfertiges Format bringen lassen. Die übrigen Funktionen zur Textnachbearbeitung bleiben erhalten."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.s1-mini-local-polish.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry s1-mini-local-polish).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Introducing \"S1-mini by Superwhisper\""
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Neu: „S1-mini von Superwhisper“"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.s1-mini-local-polish.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry s1-mini-local-polish).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "S1-mini, Superwhisper's custom-tuned local model, is now available for offline polishing. It is completely free, downloads in just 484 MB, and gives you three quick dials to shape your text: Tone, Structure, and Context. EG-1 is still the go-to for maximum polish quality, but S1-mini delivers solid on-device results on a much smaller footprint."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "S1-mini, das eigens angepasste lokale Modell von Superwhisper, ist jetzt für die Offline-Nachbearbeitung verfügbar. Es ist kostenlos, benötigt nur 484 MB Download und bietet drei schnelle Regler für deinen Text: Ton, Struktur und Kontext. EG-1 bleibt die erste Wahl für höchste Qualität, während S1-mini mit deutlich weniger Speicherbedarf gute Ergebnisse direkt auf dem Gerät liefert."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.dictionary-page-rebuilt.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry dictionary-page-rebuilt).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Re-designed Your Words into Dictionary"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Aus „Deine Wörter“ wird „Wörterbuch“"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.dictionary-page-rebuilt.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry dictionary-page-rebuilt).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "\"Your Words\" is now \"Dictionary.\" Vocab packs are fully editable, and the interface has been overhauled to make managing your custom vocabulary smoother and more intuitive."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "„Deine Wörter“ heißt jetzt „Wörterbuch“. Wortschatzpakete lassen sich vollständig bearbeiten. Die überarbeitete Oberfläche macht die Verwaltung deines eigenen Wortschatzes einfacher."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.input-channel-selection.title" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the title of one feature announcement (entry input-channel-selection).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Support for multi input devices"
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Unterstützung für Geräte mit mehreren Eingängen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.input-channel-selection.description" : {
      "comment" : "Settings > What's New: the paragraph under one feature announcement's title (entry input-channel-selection).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Multi-input audio interfaces like the Focusrite Scarlett are now properly supported. Select your specific mic input channel in microphone settings to route your audio cleanly, with no more input error messages."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Audiointerfaces mit mehreren Eingängen, etwa Focusrite Scarlett, werden jetzt richtig unterstützt. Wähle in den Mikrofoneinstellungen den gewünschten Eingangskanal aus, damit dein Audio ohne Eingabefehler ankommt."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "whatsNew.better-out-of-the-box-defaults.title" : {
